#: ../../../driver-api/80211/cfg80211.rst:97
msgid "Scanning and BSS list handling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/80211/cfg80211:99: ../include/net/cfg80211.h:2870
msgid ""
"The scanning process itself is fairly simple, but cfg80211 offers quite a "
"bit of helper functionality. To start a scan, the scan operation will be "
"invoked with a scan definition. This scan definition contains the channels "
"to scan, and the SSIDs to send probe requests for (including the wildcard, "
"if desired). A passive scan is indicated by having no SSIDs to probe. "
"Additionally, a scan request may contain extra information elements that "
"should be added to the probe request. The IEs are guaranteed to be well-"
"formed, and will not exceed the maximum length the driver advertised in the "
"wiphy structure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/80211/cfg80211:99: ../include/net/cfg80211.h:2880
msgid ""
"When scanning finds a BSS, cfg80211 needs to be notified of that, because it "
"is responsible for maintaining the BSS list; the driver should not maintain "
"a list itself. For this notification, various functions exist."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/80211/cfg80211:99: ../include/net/cfg80211.h:2884
msgid ""
"Since drivers do not maintain a BSS list, there are also a number of "
"functions to search for a BSS and obtain information about it from the BSS "
"structure cfg80211 maintains. The BSS list is also made available to "
"userspace."
msgstr ""

